  "body": "From #37. The scallop check in `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/ridge.rs` looks only within band + 3·tol of the passes, so on flat ground it sees a cusp only up to about 4·tol past the ball. #37 added a generator ceiling (stepover < ball diameter, tol < r/2), so a user can no longer state a stepover the scan can't judge. The verifier's own reach is still documented, not widened.\n\nA wider second check (re-asking within one ball diameter, needing two different passes on opposite sides) read flat rasters exactly up to s = 5.9. But it flagged false cusps under crowns and around corners in 11 finish3d fixtures: cone apex 1.68 mm, dome waterline 1.10, box walls 0.42, dome scallop 0.20, hill contour/ramp/radial about 0.18, blind pocket 0.16. The same ground M13.8's full-diameter attempt flagged.\n\nDone means: a widened reach with a rule that excludes crowns and corners, so every finish3d verdict fixture stays clean in the release lane and a flat raster past 4·tol is judged.",
